# FABLE-SONNET-UNIT-FIELD-WRITE-20260923-129 (Opus's -128 side finding). A
# method assigning a unit field declared ABOVE it used to fail translation
# SILENTLY ("translation failed with no located diagnostic"): l2_check_body
# already accepted the statement (l2_own_unit_seen, backward visibility for
# every non-callable, author 2026-09-22 blog 857692c), but l2_emit_body's
# own-field lookup for an assignment TARGET (l2_own_find_last) lacked the
# same unit-field fallback its sibling l2_own_find already had, so the name
# fell all the way through to a dead silent return: 1.
#
# Q52 (the author, 2026-09-28) cancels this row's first reading (Q9, «любое
# присвоение проецируется в поле структуры»): the name of a unit field a
# method does not declare is the method's hidden input, and a bare write
# changes only that value of its activation -- «нет видимого поля "y" у
# структуры "s"», «0 -- меняется лишь скрытый вход s».  The unit's x, y and
# z stay 5 at their place of declaration, read here through gx, gy and gz
# (node\x): the root's own bare x would read its working value 5 either way,
# not reloaded after a call (book §12), so it could not tell.  A method that
# means to change them writes node\x explicitly.
#
# Three shapes: write from a method; write then read within the same method,
# same activation (8 there); write from inside a nested if body within the
# method (the write does not care which control-flow depth it runs at).
int: x 5
int: y 5

fn: bump () int
    x: 7
    return: 0
end: bump

fn: bump_and_read () int
    y: 8
    if: y != 8
        return: 1
    return: 0
end: bump_and_read

int: z 5
fn: bump_nested () int
    if: 1 != 0
        z: 9
    return: 0
end: bump_nested

fn: gx () int
    int: v 0
    v: node\x
    return: v
end: gx

fn: gy () int
    int: v 0
    v: node\y
    return: v
end: gy

fn: gz () int
    int: v 0
    v: node\z
    return: v
end: gz

int: r
int: seen 0
bump()
seen: gx()
if: seen != 5
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 90; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
r: bump_and_read()
if: r != 0
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 91; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
seen: gy()
if: seen != 5
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 93; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
bump_nested()
seen: gz()
if: seen != 5
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 92; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 0; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
